# Third-party licenses

phonia itself is dual-licensed, `MIT OR Apache-2.0` — see [LICENSE-MIT](LICENSE-MIT)
and [LICENSE-APACHE](LICENSE-APACHE). This file covers the third-party crates
compiled into its binaries, whose licenses require their copyright notices to be
reproduced wherever those binaries are distributed.

It is **generated**, never edited by hand:

```sh
cargo about generate about.hbs > THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md
```

Dynamically linked system libraries are not listed here, since they are not
distributed with phonia. The one that matters is `libasound` (alsa-lib),
LGPL-2.1-or-later: linking it dynamically satisfies the LGPL on its own, and a
package that bundles it statically would have obligations this file does not cover.

